Security and no-claim proof for WP09:

Passed by TypeScript/Rust tests:
- foreground evidence rejects content knowledge claims;
- background rows cannot claim open foreground focus;
- background process rows can carry zero foreground duration;
- foreground duration is clamped so it cannot exceed running duration when
  applied to runtime summaries;
- title refs are only accepted when titleCaptureState is titleRef;
- omitted titles remain explicit;
- permission-limited foreground metadata remains explicit;
- unknown foreground process is not promoted to known app without deterministic
  refs;
- launcher foreground focus remains knownLauncher, not active game proof.

Not claimed:
- no content capture;
- no screen capture;
- no message/feed/document/video knowledge;
- no live OS polling;
- no policy execution;
- no broad blocking.
